<h1>Reform options: what changes, and who gains or loses</h1>

<p class="lede">Two separate decisions are often discussed together. One is how the State Pension should rise each year. The other is who should be entitled to it. This page sets out the options for each, the evidence on costs and on who is affected, and the points where the answer depends on a judgement about fairness.</p>

{% call m.note("How to read this page", 2) %}
<p>The page asks the same questions of every option, including keeping the present rule. Where the evidence is strong, the page says so. Where a claim is a recommendation or a value judgement, the page says whose it is. It recommends no option.</p>
{% endcall %}

{% call m.note("A change was announced on " ~ (("pm-care-2026-09-29" | sourceRecord).published_date | timeTag), 2) %}
<p>{{ ("tl-kept-to-2030" | claim).statement }} {{ ("rule-2030" | claim).statement }} {{ ("ncs-savings-used" | claim).statement }} {{ m.c("rule-2030") }}</p>
<p>This is an announcement. It is not law. {{ ("rule-2030-legislate" | claim).statement }} The options on this page are still the ones to compare, and <a href="#opt-2030">the announced rule</a> is now one of them. <a href="#social-care">Pensions and social care</a> sets out the plan and what it leaves open.</p>
{% endcall %}

